INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "Mandiant: Zero-Day Vulnerability in MOVEit Transfer Exploited for Data Theft", "source_url": "https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa23-158a", "text": "SRC-001 reports that Progress announced the MOVEit Transfer zero-day on May 31, 2023 and it was assigned CVE-2023-34362. Mandiant found earliest exploitation evidence on May 27, 2023, involving deployment of web shells and data theft; some theft occurred within minutes. The newly discovered C# web shell LEMURLOOT masqueraded as human.aspx, with variants human2.aspx and _human2.aspx. It could enumerate files/folders, retrieve configuration and Azure Blob credentials/settings, retrieve files, and create/delete a Health Check Service user. Exploitation involved POST requests to guestaccess.aspx consistent with SQL injection. Scanning/exploitation often came from 5.252.188.0/22; second-stage activity used different systems, many with RDP certificates generated May 19-22. The campaign affected organizations in Canada, India, and the U.S., with public repository samples suggesting Italy, Pakistan, and Germany; Mandiant said impact was likely broader. Mandiant initially attributed activity to UNC4857, then on June 6 merged UNC4857 into FIN11 based on targeting, infrastructure, certificate, and data leak site overlaps. Mandiant described the activity as consistent with extortion actors and prior FIN11-attributed file-transfer exploitation, including Accellion FTA/DEWMODE and GoAnywhere CVE-2023-0669. On June 5 Bleeping Computer reportedly said a CLOP-affiliated person claimed responsibility; on June 6 the CL0P^_-LEAKS data leak site claimed responsibility and threatened publication absent payment. Mandiant had not directly observed extortion emails to confirmed victims; delayed ransom emails were presented as plausible based on prior FIN11 behavior, not as confirmed fact. SRC-002 (NVD) describes CVE-2023-34362 as an unauthenticated SQL injection in MOVEit Transfer allowing database access and potentially SQL statements that alter/delete database elements; exploitation in the wild in May and June 2023 via HTTP/HTTPS; NVD published date June 2, 2023; CISA KEV added date June 2 and due date June 23, 2023."}
